\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Hardware Grover-primitive certification. (a) Success probability at the best iteration count on \texttt  {ibm\_marrakesh} (released code, $n{=}4$--$9$, run truncated at $n{=}9$ by an account usage limit) and on the earlier \texttt  {ibm\_fez} run ($n{=}4$--$12$), with the $k{=}0$ control near the random baseline; the \texttt  {ibm\_fez} run reaches the noise wall at $n\!\ge \!11$. (b) The \texttt  {ibm\_fez} iteration sweep: the textbook $k^{*}$ collapses first, $k_{\mathrm  {adp}}$ next, while $k{=}1$ stays optimal across the usable regime.}}{8}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
